      housing: "Build the house around the back. Ramps or steps at every surface the dog wants to be on, baby gates at the top and bottom of stairs, and rugs or runners on any slick floor where a landing could go wrong. Jumping down from a sofa is the single most common household movement that precipitates a disc episode, so the goal is to remove the opportunity rather than train the dog out of wanting it. Walk on a harness, never a neck collar: a Dachshund that lunges on a collar loads the cervical spine, and cervical discs are the second most common site after the thoracolumbar junction.",
