      enrichment: "This is a scent hound with a working brain, and the frustration of an under-stimulated Dachshund shows up as digging, barking, and destructive behavior long before it shows up as boredom. Scent work suits them exactly: snuffle mats, hide-and-find games, and formal nose work all satisfy the original job without asking the spine to do anything athletic. Keep the exercise low-impact and level. Steady walks are excellent. Repeated jumping, stair sprints, and hard twisting play are not.",
